<title>HUNGARY: FORECAST - Hungary T-bill yields seen down this week.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Hungary T-bill yields seen down this week.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungarian discount Treasury-bills were expected to drop at this week's auctions, dealers said on Monday.</p>
<p>The Government Debt Management agency will auction one-month T-bills on Tuesday, three-month bills on Wednesday, Six-month bills on Thursday and 12-month bills on Friday.</p>
<p>		  ONE-MONTH   THREE-MONTH   SIX-MONTH    12-MONTH</p>
<p> Bills offered   1		 5	     12	    14</p>
<p>(HUF billion)</p>
<p>Average yield at</p>
<p>  last auction  21.73	   21.30	  21.07	 20.85</p>
<p>Valid bid</p>
<p>  range     19.73-22.73   19.30-21.80  19.07-21.57  18.85-21.35</p>
<p>FORECASTS OF HUNGARIAN DEALERS</p>
<p>Zoltan Bereczki/Bank Austria -GiroCredit</p>
<p>    AVERAGE     21.6	    21.2	   20.9	  20.6</p>
<p>    MAXIMUM     21.8	    21.4	   21.1	  20.8</p>
<p>Gyula Kerdo/Creditanstalt Securities</p>
<p>    AVERAGE     21.77	   21.17	  20.92	 20.66</p>
<p>    MAXIMUM     21.85	   21.31	  21.13	 20.91</p>
<p>Zsolt Bango/Gog Securities</p>
<p>    AVERAGE     21.6	    20.9	   20.7	  20.45</p>
<p>    MAXIMUM     21.85	   21.1	   20.9	  20.65</p>
<p>-- Sandor Peto, Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
</text>
